# Line endings for this repository.
#
# The transport repo gets its own copy of this, shipped as toolkit/gitattributes
# and installed by bootstrap.sh. This one covers the skill repo, so that a
# contributor working on Windows cannot commit a toolkit script with CRLF in it
# and ship the breakage to every transport repo bootstrapped afterwards.
#
# The failure it prevents is documented in full in toolkit/gitattributes. The
# short version: Git for Windows' bash tolerates CRLF perfectly well, so the
# harm is never to the Windows machine that produced it - it is to every Linux
# clone afterwards, where a sourced CRLF file does not stop, it silently loses
# `set -uo pipefail`.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Shipped without a dot on purpose; still a shell-adjacent text file.
gitignore     text eol=lf
gitattributes text eol=lf
